  "question": {
    "text": "A block of mass m attached to a massless spring is performing oscillatory motion of amplitude &#39;A&#39; on a frictionless horizontal plane. If half of the mass of the block breaks off when it is passing through its equilibrium point, the amplitude of oscillation for the remaining system become &fnof;A. The value of &fnof; is:"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></mfrac></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "D"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Using mometum conservation&nbsp;</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"/><mi>m</mi><mi>A</mi><mi>&#969;</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi>&#969;</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"/><mi>m</mi><mi>A</mi><msqrt><mfrac><mi>k</mi><mi>m</mi></mfrac></msqrt><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msqrt><mfrac><mi>k</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></msqrt><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"/><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt><mi>A</mi><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></math></p>"
